values
  ('agent_tool:check_audit_status', 'Real prospect/website audit status', 'Currently-stored public_audit_requests rows for a tenant -- business name, website URL, status, job_status, progress_percentage, requested product, timestamps. The exact same data app/api/platform/audit/route.ts''s GET (list) handler returns, scoped by tenantId instead of a cookie session.', 'audit', 'audit status read', 'check_audit_status', 'app/api/platform/audit/route.ts (public_audit_requests table)', 'Engineering', null, 'agent:read:audit_reports', 'read', 'tenant', 'free', 'read', 'none (read-only)', 'REAL_EXPOSED', 'Deliberately its own permission (agent:read:audit_reports), distinct from the pre-existing agent:read:audit which gates inspect_audit_events (the platform''s own internal security/action log) -- same word, unrelated data, never conflated. packages/audit-engine''s runAutomaticAuditGeneration pipeline itself (AUDIT_ENGINE_MODE defaults to disabled per that route''s own comment) stays untraced/unbridged this pass -- this tool only reads already-persisted request/job rows, never triggers generation.', null, now(), 'claude_session_2026-09-02');
